"SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>DAICEL CHEM</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>INOUE SATOSHI</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>TANAKA YOSHIKAZU</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>DAICEL CHEMICAL INDUSTRIES, LTD.</last-name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>INOUE, SATOSHI</last-name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>TANAKA, YOSHIKAZU</last-name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>INOUE SATOSHI</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>TANAKA YOSHIKAZU</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>INOUE, SATOSHI</last-name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>TANAKA, YOSHIKAZU</last-name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A touch panel comprises a substrate (11) capable of propagating sound waves and a transducer (13a) mounted on the substrate to send or receive sound waves. The substrate (11) includes rounded edges (16) at its corners so that sound waves may propagate from the front to back or back to front of the substrate (11). The transducer (13a), mounted on the back of the substrate (11), receives the sound waves propagating via the rounded edges. The radius of curvature (R) of the rounded edges (16) of the substrate (11) is greater than 0.5 mm. Such a touch panel has a simplified structure, prevents projections from appearing on the surface of the propagation medium, and increases adaptability to thinner LCD monitors.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne un écran tactile comprenant un substrat (11) capable de propager des ondes sonores, et un transducteur (13a) monté sur le substrat pour envoyer ou recevoir des ondes sonores. Le substrat (11) comprend des bords arrondis (16) sur ses angles de sorte que les ondes sonores puissent se propager de l'avant du substrat (11) à l'arrière et inversement. Le transducteur (13a), monté sur l'arrière du substrat (11), reçoit les ondes sonores se propageant via les bords arrondis. Le rayon de courbure (R) des bords arrondis (16) du substrat (11) est supérieur à 0,5mm. Un tel écran tactile présente une structure simplifiée, empêche la formation de projections sur la surface du support de propagation, et augmente l'adaptabilité avec des moniteurs LCD plus minces.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>